course: dictionary
lesson: 13810
title: Irrational: not based on good reasons
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Irrational means not based on clear thinking or good reasons. A fear is irrational when it is much bigger than any real danger, or when there is no danger at all. «Sam had an irrational fear of spiders, even tiny ones in a book.» The clue is the word fear: Sam's fear does not match what could really happen.
explain: «It was irrational to shout at the bus, because the bus cannot hear you.» Shouting at a bus does not make sense, so irrational means not sensible. Ask yourself: is there a good reason for this? If there is not, irrational may fit.
explain: Maths uses the word too, with a clear meaning. Rational numbers can be written as fractions. An irrational number cannot, and its decimals go on forever without repeating. «Pi is an irrational number.»
fact: Irrational means not based on clear thinking or good reasons.
fact: The opposite in everyday use is rational, which means sensible and based on good reasons.
fact: «An irrational fear» is a fear that is out of proportion to the real danger, or has no real reason.
fact: In maths, an irrational number cannot be written as a fraction of two whole numbers.
fact: Pi and the square root of 2 are irrational numbers: their decimals go on forever without repeating.
exercise: «Sam had an irrational fear of spiders, even tiny ones in a book.» What does irrational mean here? | Written down in a book | *Not based on good reasons | Very big and strong | Happy and calm
exercise: Which of these is an irrational number? | *pi | 1/2 | 3 | 0.75
exercise: «It was irrational to shout at the bus, because the bus cannot hear you.» Is shouting at the bus irrational or rational? | *Irrational | Clever | Rational, because buses like noise | Kind
test: «He stayed home all day, afraid the sun would fall out of the sky.» Why is this fear irrational? | *The fear has no good reason behind it | It is about a fish | It is a sensible way to stay safe
test: Which number cannot be written as a fraction of two whole numbers? | 0.5 | 3/4 | *square root of 2 | 7
exam: What does irrational mean in «an irrational choice made in anger»? | *Not based on clear thinking or good reasons | Made by a very clever person | Made with clear thinking and good reasons | Long and slow
